<div class="container masterplan">
<h1 id="top">AI Power Sources Plan</h1>
<div class="last-updated doc-muted">Created: 2026-11-12 | Version: 0.1 | Status: PLAN (todo #2742, project 5, schema branch)</div>
<p class="mp-back-link"><a href="/Documentation/SchemaMasterPlan">← Schema Master Plan</a></p>

<h2>1. Summary</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Problem.</strong> Comserv has no record of how AI providers power their compute. Spend cannot be steered to cleaner providers.</li>
<li><strong>Evidence.</strong> No <code>power</code>/<code>energy</code>/<code>provider</code> table in Ency (grep of <code>table()</code> names, 2026-11-12). Providers exist only as slugs: <code>ai_model_policy.provider</code> (e.g. supergrok, openrouter, ollama). <code>ai_model_config</code> is per site/role/model config, not a provider registry.</li>
<li><strong>Impact.</strong> The router picks models on cost/policy only. Facts on power (IEA mix, nuclear deals, onsite gas) live in chat, not data.</li>
<li><strong>Solution.</strong> Four new Result files: <code>ai_providers</code>, <code>ai_sites</code>, <code>ai_power_sources</code>, <code>ai_energy_metrics</code>. Tables made only by schema compare "Create Table". Seed only cited rows through the app.</li>
<li><strong>Risk / undo.</strong> New tables only; no existing table changes. Undo = drop the four empty tables via schema compare and revert the commit. Live DB 192.168.1.20:3307 is the only DB; Shanta clicks each create.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Conventions used</h2>
<ul>
<li>Style from <code>Result/HealthKitchen/IntakeLog.pm</code>: <code>load_components('InflateColumn::DateTime','TimeStamp')</code>, <code>sitename varchar(255) NOT NULL</code>, <code>created_at/updated_at datetime</code> with <code>set_on_create/set_on_update</code>.</li>
<li>Enum-like values are <code>varchar</code> + <code>documentation</code> (as <code>AiModelPolicy.status</code>). New values need no ALTER.</li>
<li>No <code>add_index</code> in this DBIC; only <code>add_unique_constraint</code>. Create Table uses SQL::Translator per table, so <code>belongs_to</code> adds FK + index on <code>provider_id</code>/<code>site_id</code>.</li>
<li>Size: Util/Model/Result ≤800 lines soft, Controllers ≤2,000 soft (SchemaSystemPlan / MASTER_PLAN).</li>
<li>Logging via <code>log_with_details</code>; no inline JS; changelog fragments only (AGENTS.md, .hermes.md §4).</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Reuse decision</h2>
<p>No provider table exists, so <code>ai_providers</code> is new and is the FK target. Its <code>slug</code> equals the Router billing slug in <code>ai_model_policy.provider</code> — a soft join, no FK, no change to existing tables. <code>ai_model_config</code> is left alone (many rows per provider; changing it needs Shanta's OK).</p>

<h2>4. Tables (field lists)</h2>
<p>All: <code>id</code> int AI PK, <code>sitename</code> varchar(255) NOT NULL, <code>created_at</code>/<code>updated_at</code> datetime NULL (auto).</p>
<h3>ai_providers (AiProvider.pm)</h3>
<ul>
<li>slug varchar(50) NOT NULL — router billing slug</li>
<li>name varchar(100) NOT NULL; company varchar(100) NULL; model_family varchar(100) NULL</li>
<li>api_endpoint varchar(500) NULL — reference only, never a key</li>
<li>preferred_rank int NULL — 1 = most preferred for clean power; NULL = unranked</li>
<li>notes text NULL; last_updated date NULL</li>
<li>Unique <code>ai_providers_site_slug (sitename, slug)</code>. has_many sites, power_sources, energy_metrics (cascade_delete 0).</li>
</ul>
<h3>ai_sites (AiSite.pm) — data centers</h3>
<ul>
<li>provider_id int NOT NULL → ai_providers.id</li>
<li>name varchar(150) NOT NULL; location varchar(255) NULL; country_code varchar(2) NULL; grid_region varchar(100) NULL</li>
<li>status varchar(20) NOT NULL default 'unknown' — planned|construction|operating|retired|unknown</li>
<li>estimated_mw decimal(10,2) NULL; source_url varchar(500) NULL; notes text NULL</li>
<li>Unique <code>ai_sites_provider_name (provider_id, name)</code>. belongs_to provider; has_many power_sources, energy_metrics.</li>
</ul>
<h3>ai_power_sources (AiPowerSource.pm)</h3>
<ul>
<li>provider_id int NULL, site_id int NULL — at least one set (checked in Util)</li>
<li>source_type varchar(20) NOT NULL — nuclear|gas|coal|solar|wind|hydro|grid_mix|fuel_cell|other|unknown</li>
<li>capacity_mw decimal(10,2) NULL</li>
<li>basis varchar(12) NOT NULL — physical|contractual (PPA/REC ≠ physical)</li>
<li>status varchar(20) NOT NULL default 'operating' — planned|contracted|operating|retired</li>
<li>start_year int NULL; end_year int NULL</li>
<li>source_url varchar(500) NOT NULL; source_title varchar(255) NULL</li>
<li>confidence varchar(10) NOT NULL default 'medium' — high|medium|low; last_verified date NULL; notes text NULL</li>
<li>belongs_to provider, site (LEFT).</li>
</ul>
<h3>ai_energy_metrics (AiEnergyMetric.pm) — mix shares over time</h3>
<ul>
<li>provider_id int NULL, site_id int NULL</li>
<li>scope varchar(20) NOT NULL default 'provider' — global|country|provider|site (IEA global/US mix = global/country rows)</li>
<li>country_code varchar(2) NULL; metric_date date NOT NULL (period start); period varchar(10) NOT NULL default 'year' — year|month|day|hour</li>
<li>basis varchar(12) NOT NULL — physical|contractual</li>
<li>renewable_pct_annual, renewable_pct_hourly, nuclear_pct, gas_pct, coal_pct decimal(5,2) NULL</li>
<li>nuclear_mw, gas_mw decimal(10,2) NULL</li>
<li>source_url varchar(500) NOT NULL; source_title varchar(255) NULL; notes text NULL</li>
<li>belongs_to provider, site (LEFT).</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Seed-data rule</h2>
<p>Every power-source and metric row needs <code>source_url</code>, <code>basis</code> and <code>confidence</code>. No invented numbers. Enter through the app (prompt 3), never SQL. Candidate sources (from Shanta's research, to be verified at entry): IEA <em>Energy and AI</em> mix (global, US); Microsoft–Constellation Crane restart; Amazon–Talen Susquehanna; Meta–Vistra; Google–Kairos; xAI Colossus permits.</p>

<h2>6. Multi-site</h2>
<p>Every table has <code>sitename</code> like other Ency tables. Seed under <code>CSC</code>. A site's <code>preferred_rank</code> is its own; facts may be copied per site later if needed (open question).</p>

<h2>7. Router handoff (aisystem branch — describe only)</h2>
<p>Router reads <code>ai_providers.preferred_rank</code> by <code>(sitename, slug = billing provider)</code>, falling back to <code>CSC</code>. Use it only as a tie-breaker after kill-switch and <code>ai_model_policy</code> status. NULL rank = no effect. Cache per request. Owner: Chat-with-AI fixer on <code>aisystem</code>.</p>

<h2>8. AI editor prompts</h2>
<h3>Prompt 1 — Result files only</h3>
<pre class="doc-pre">TASK (Comserv2, schema branch, worktree ~/.comserv/worktrees/schema/Comserv): create FOUR new DBIx::Class Result files for AI power-source data. New files only. Do not edit any existing file. No SQL, no migrations, no scripts, no deploy. Plan: /Documentation/AiPowerSourcesPlan (todo #2742).

Before you start: git status (stop and report if there is uncommitted work you did not make), then git merge main.

Conventions (copy from lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HealthKitchen/IntakeLog.pm):
- use strict; use warnings; use base &#x27;DBIx::Class::Core&#x27;;
- __PACKAGE__-&gt;load_components(&#x27;InflateColumn::DateTime&#x27;, &#x27;TimeStamp&#x27;);
- id integer is_auto_increment PK; sitename varchar 255 NOT NULL
- created_at datetime nullable set_on_create =&gt; 1; updated_at datetime nullable set_on_create =&gt; 1, set_on_update =&gt; 1
- Enum-like columns are varchar + a &#x27;documentation&#x27; attribute listing the allowed values (same as AiModelPolicy.status). Do NOT use data_type &#x27;enum&#x27;.
- No add_index in this DBIC version. Only add_unique_constraint(name =&gt; [cols]). FK indexes come from belongs_to.
- Decimal sizes are arrays: size =&gt; [10, 2].
- Each file ends with 1; and stays well under 800 lines.

Files (all under Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/):

1) AiProvider.pm  package Comserv::Model::Schema::Ency::Result::AiProvider  table ai_providers
   id; sitename;
   slug varchar 50 NOT NULL (documentation: same slug the AI Router uses as billing provider, e.g. supergrok, openrouter, ollama; matches ai_model_policy.provider);
   name varchar 100 NOT NULL; company varchar 100 NULL; model_family varchar 100 NULL;
   api_endpoint varchar 500 NULL (documentation: reference URL only, never a key);
   preferred_rank integer NULL (documentation: 1 = most preferred for clean power; NULL = unranked);
   notes text NULL; last_updated date NULL; created_at; updated_at.
   PK id. add_unique_constraint(ai_providers_site_slug =&gt; [qw(sitename slug)]).
   has_many sites =&gt; AiSite provider_id; has_many power_sources =&gt; AiPowerSource provider_id; has_many energy_metrics =&gt; AiEnergyMetric provider_id. Use cascade_delete =&gt; 0 on each has_many.

2) AiSite.pm  package ...::AiSite  table ai_sites
   id; sitename; provider_id integer NOT NULL; name varchar 150 NOT NULL;
   location varchar 255 NULL; country_code varchar 2 NULL; grid_region varchar 100 NULL;
   status varchar 20 NOT NULL default &#x27;unknown&#x27; (documentation: planned|construction|operating|retired|unknown);
   estimated_mw decimal [10,2] NULL; source_url varchar 500 NULL; notes text NULL; created_at; updated_at.
   PK id. add_unique_constraint(ai_sites_provider_name =&gt; [qw(provider_id name)]).
   belongs_to provider =&gt; AiProvider { &#x27;foreign.id&#x27; =&gt; &#x27;self.provider_id&#x27; }.
   has_many power_sources =&gt; AiPowerSource site_id; has_many energy_metrics =&gt; AiEnergyMetric site_id (cascade_delete =&gt; 0).

3) AiPowerSource.pm  package ...::AiPowerSource  table ai_power_sources
   id; sitename; provider_id integer NULL; site_id integer NULL (documentation: at least one of provider_id/site_id is set; checked in code later);
   source_type varchar 20 NOT NULL (documentation: nuclear|gas|coal|solar|wind|hydro|grid_mix|fuel_cell|other|unknown);
   capacity_mw decimal [10,2] NULL;
   basis varchar 12 NOT NULL (documentation: physical|contractual — physical = electrons actually used; contractual = PPA/REC);
   status varchar 20 NOT NULL default &#x27;operating&#x27; (documentation: planned|contracted|operating|retired);
   start_year integer NULL; end_year integer NULL;
   source_url varchar 500 NOT NULL; source_title varchar 255 NULL;
   confidence varchar 10 NOT NULL default &#x27;medium&#x27; (documentation: high|medium|low);
   last_verified date NULL; notes text NULL; created_at; updated_at.
   PK id. belongs_to provider =&gt; AiProvider (provider_id) and site =&gt; AiSite (site_id), both with { join_type =&gt; &#x27;LEFT&#x27; }.

4) AiEnergyMetric.pm  package ...::AiEnergyMetric  table ai_energy_metrics
   id; sitename; provider_id integer NULL; site_id integer NULL;
   scope varchar 20 NOT NULL default &#x27;provider&#x27; (documentation: global|country|provider|site; global/country rows have no provider/site);
   country_code varchar 2 NULL; metric_date date NOT NULL (documentation: start of the period);
   period varchar 10 NOT NULL default &#x27;year&#x27; (documentation: year|month|day|hour);
   basis varchar 12 NOT NULL (physical|contractual);
   renewable_pct_annual decimal [5,2] NULL; renewable_pct_hourly decimal [5,2] NULL;
   nuclear_pct decimal [5,2] NULL; gas_pct decimal [5,2] NULL; coal_pct decimal [5,2] NULL;
   nuclear_mw decimal [10,2] NULL; gas_mw decimal [10,2] NULL;
   source_url varchar 500 NOT NULL; source_title varchar 255 NULL; notes text NULL; created_at; updated_at.
   PK id. belongs_to provider and site as in AiPowerSource (LEFT).

Relationship class names are the full package, e.g. &#x27;Comserv::Model::Schema::Ency::Result::AiSite&#x27;.

Checks before you report:
- From Comserv/: perl -Ilib -Ilocal/lib/perl5 -c on each new file -&gt; syntax OK.
- perl -Ilib -Ilocal/lib/perl5 -MComserv::Model::Schema::Ency -e &#x27;my $s=&quot;Comserv::Model::Schema::Ency&quot;; print join(&quot;,&quot;, grep { /^Ai(Provider|Site|PowerSource|EnergyMetric)$/ } $s-&gt;sources), &quot;\n&quot;&#x27; lists all four (if the schema loads namespaces that way; if not, report what you ran).
- git add only the four files, commit small on schema: &quot;feat(schema): Result files for AI power-source data (#2742)&quot;. Add a changelog fragment Comserv/root/Documentation/changelog/entries/YYYY-MM-DD-ai-power-sources-results.inc. Do not push.
- Report: commit hash, perl -c output, file paths.

Then Shanta (not the editor) does: restart :4007 herself if the new classes do not show, open http://workstation.local:4007/admin/schema_compare -&gt; db-server-1:3307 -&gt; ency -&gt; &quot;Result files without tables&quot;. Create in this order: ai_providers, ai_sites, ai_power_sources, ai_energy_metrics. Read each proposed CREATE before confirming (expect varchar not enum, decimal(10,2)/(5,2), the two unique keys, FK keys on provider_id/site_id). After create, the tables list should show all four with the OK badge (0 issues). Any issue count above 0: copy the issue text to chat.

Policy: Result file is the schema truth; never hand DDL; log_with_details in every catch (later code); no inline JS; new files only; no server restarts by the editor; live DB writes only through Shanta&#x27;s schema-compare click.
</pre>
<h3>Prompt 2 — outline</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>Comserv/Util/AI/PowerSources.pm</code> (≤800 lines): list/get/save per table, value checks (allowed values, one of provider_id/site_id, pct 0–100, source_url required), <code>log_with_details</code> in every catch.</li>
<li><code>Controller/Admin/AiPower.pm</code>: list/view/edit for providers, sites, power sources, metrics; admin role check; CSRF as other admin forms.</li>
<li>Templates <code>root/admin/ai_power/*.tt</code>; JS <code>root/static/js/admin/ai-power.js</code> via <code>js_load.tt</code>; CSS with <code>var(--*)</code>; no inline JS.</li>
<li>Tests <code>t/ai_power_sources.t</code> for the checks. Changelog fragment. Commit small.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Prompt 3 — outline</h3>
<ul>
<li>Seed through the prompt-2 UI only, one row per cited fact; open each source first; fill source_url, source_title, basis, confidence, last_verified.</li>
<li>Skip any number the source does not state. Report a table of rows added with URLs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Hermes fix-prompt template</h2>
<pre class="doc-pre">FIX: [error text / page / log line]
Rules: work only in ~/.comserv/worktrees/schema/Comserv (branch schema, port 4007).
1. git status; stop if foreign uncommitted work. git merge main.
2. Diagnose from logs (Comserv/logs/, dev_server_4007.log) and the code path. State the root cause.
3. Fix the root cause in the smallest change. No SQL, migrations or scripts. Live DB 192.168.1.20:3307 read-only. No deploy. No server restarts unless Shanta asks.
4. perl -c changed files; run related tests (prove -Ilib -Ilocal/lib/perl5 t/...).
5. Commit small with a changelog fragment. Log against todo #[id].
6. Report: cause, files changed, commit hash, test output, what Shanta should click to verify.</pre>

<h2>10. Open questions</h2>
<ul>
<li>Is one provider row per router billing slug right? OpenRouter resells other labs, so its power is the upstream lab's.</li>
<li>Per-site rows, or one global CSC set for all sites?</li>
<li>Rank by hand, or compute from metrics later?</li>
</ul>
</div>
